1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:01,619
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,621 --> 00:00:03,013
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,205 --> 00:00:05,305
(Episode 79)

4
00:00:09,338 --> 00:00:10,420
Are you tired?

5
00:00:42,472 --> 00:00:44,311
- Honey.
- Yeah?

6
00:00:44,352 --> 00:00:45,352
Wake up.

7
00:00:53,139 --> 00:00:55,471
So this is what a sunrise looks like.

8
00:00:56,199 --> 00:00:57,373
I want to paint it.

9
00:01:00,698 --> 00:01:02,890
That's you. Always thinking about art.

10
00:01:15,978 --> 00:01:17,992
This is so nice. I love it.

11
00:01:27,351 --> 00:01:29,147
It's hot!

12
00:01:29,358 --> 00:01:31,925
Are you stupid? Why would you eat it
just because I gave it to you?

13
00:01:31,958 --> 00:01:33,236
You have to check if it's too hot first.

14
00:01:33,238 --> 00:01:35,242
I thought you'd already checked
if it was too hot.

15
00:01:38,457 --> 00:01:39,663
It's not that hot.

16
00:01:47,078 --> 00:01:49,525
- I'll get even when I'm back in Seoul.
- Get even for what?

17
00:01:49,882 --> 00:01:52,545
Mom and Jung A are going to pay
for ruining my wedding night.

18
00:01:53,598 --> 00:01:55,007
Your mom was pretty cute, though.

19
00:01:55,009 --> 00:01:56,318
What's cute about her?

20
00:01:56,845 --> 00:02:00,185
I've heard of mothers-in-law
crashing honeymoons,

21
00:02:00,219 --> 00:02:02,422
but never the bride's own mom
being the villain.

22
00:02:02,643 --> 00:02:03,643
Villain?

23
00:02:03,729 --> 00:02:05,646
- That was harsh.
- What was?

24
00:02:05,648 --> 00:02:07,585
She's a villain. Always has been.

25
00:02:10,538 --> 00:02:12,775
Jeon Jung A,
just wait till you get married.

26
00:02:14,131 --> 00:02:15,743
I'll pay you back in kind.

27
00:02:16,652 --> 00:02:17,943
Honey, do you hold a grudge?

28
00:02:21,492 --> 00:02:23,712
I didn't think I did, but maybe I do.

29
00:02:24,258 --> 00:02:28,034
When I was Na Ji Ni, Na Se Ri's daughter,
I kept my head down and let things slide,

30
00:02:28,228 --> 00:02:29,315
but now I want to speak up.

31
00:02:30,372 --> 00:02:32,440
Because I'm Lim Ji Hu's wife, Na Ji Ni.

32
00:02:34,235 --> 00:02:35,341
Am I being childish?

33
00:02:35,754 --> 00:02:37,461
No. I feel for you.

34
00:02:38,538 --> 00:02:40,183
I'll always be on your side.

35
00:02:41,712 --> 00:02:43,973
I never thought I'd say
something like that.

36
00:02:44,554 --> 00:02:45,639
It feels strange.

37
00:02:46,618 --> 00:02:50,332
But when you're focused,
your mouth makes a little triangle.

38
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:51,900
It's cute.

39
00:02:52,665 --> 00:02:54,983
You're the first person besides my dad
to say that.

40
00:02:55,918 --> 00:02:58,482
Your dad and I are the only men
who've ever looked at you...

41
00:02:58,550 --> 00:03:00,081
with love in our eyes.

42
00:03:03,192 --> 00:03:05,898
- Hurry up and eat!
- You're cute.

43
00:03:13,204 --> 00:03:15,759
Looks like your daughter's husband
is doing pretty well.

44
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:16,992
Look at all those flower stands.

45
00:03:17,012 --> 00:03:18,012
You.

46
00:03:18,290 --> 00:03:21,065
Go near my daughter, and I'll kill you.

47
00:03:25,578 --> 00:03:26,892
I can't keep going like this.

48
00:03:27,652 --> 00:03:29,992
I can't let him keep pushing me around.

49
00:03:30,247 --> 00:03:31,247
The police...

50
00:03:34,852 --> 00:03:37,663
What am I supposed to do?

51
00:03:38,758 --> 00:03:40,285
You're only eating now?

52
00:03:41,972 --> 00:03:43,232
Yeong Ju, what brings you here?

53
00:03:44,378 --> 00:03:47,544
You looked really rough at the wedding.

54
00:03:48,885 --> 00:03:50,122
I had this medicine prepared.

55
00:03:50,725 --> 00:03:54,312
I gave Sa Bin the money,
so make sure you take it.

56
00:03:56,805 --> 00:03:57,805
Yeong Ju.

57
00:03:58,450 --> 00:04:00,368
Why are you being so nice to me?

58
00:04:01,111 --> 00:04:03,350
I know. Why am I?

59
00:04:06,298 --> 00:04:07,573
Seeing you send your daughter off...

60
00:04:07,894 --> 00:04:11,125
all alone, without a husband,
really tugged at my heart.

61
00:04:13,725 --> 00:04:15,852
What's gotten into you? Are you crying?

62
00:04:16,223 --> 00:04:17,772
Are you that touched?

63
00:04:18,995 --> 00:04:21,338
I don't know. Stop being so nice to me.

64
00:04:21,425 --> 00:04:25,449
I'm all alone now. If you keep being
this nice to me, I'll lose my mind.

65
00:04:25,451 --> 00:04:27,241
We're supposed to be enemies.

66
00:04:27,242 --> 00:04:29,016
I know, right?

67
00:04:31,065 --> 00:04:33,554
Your menopause must be hitting you hard.

68
00:04:33,556 --> 00:04:34,885
I don't know!

69
00:04:35,298 --> 00:04:37,808
Stop being nice!
I don't want to apologize to you.

70
00:04:39,278 --> 00:04:41,078
Who asked you to apologize?

71
00:04:41,378 --> 00:04:44,056
I just wanted to say you did well
sending Ji Ni off. That's all.

72
00:04:44,058 --> 00:04:45,478
Why are you reading so much into it?

73
00:04:46,118 --> 00:04:47,316
Stop being nice to me.

74
00:04:47,318 --> 00:04:51,597
Even if you keep being this sweet to me,
there's nothing I can do for you now.

75
00:04:53,144 --> 00:04:54,511
What are you talking about?

76
00:04:56,092 --> 00:04:58,243
I'm not here to tell you to move out.

77
00:04:58,245 --> 00:04:59,985
Stay here even after Ji Ni leaves.

78
00:04:59,998 --> 00:05:01,829
Ji Ni needs a home to come back to.

79
00:05:01,916 --> 00:05:03,338
Take care of yourself.

80
00:05:04,173 --> 00:05:06,406
And she needs a mother she can rely on.

81
00:05:13,445 --> 00:05:14,445
By the way,

82
00:05:15,108 --> 00:05:17,149
I heard you sent 100,000 dollars
as wedding gifts.

83
00:05:18,558 --> 00:05:20,048
Didn't you say you were broke?

84
00:05:21,504 --> 00:05:22,504
Yeah.

85
00:05:23,292 --> 00:05:26,527
Good thing I left everything I'd set aside
for the kids' weddings untouched.

86
00:05:27,883 --> 00:05:28,883
Yeong Ju.

87
00:05:29,145 --> 00:05:31,078
I never realized it when I was alone,

88
00:05:31,627 --> 00:05:34,344
but getting remarried
really changes how you feel.

89
00:05:35,476 --> 00:05:37,320
Is this what married life is like?

90
00:05:39,692 --> 00:05:42,275
When Ji Ni gets here,
be a good mother-in-law.

91
00:05:43,647 --> 00:05:44,647
I'm heading out.

92
00:05:52,792 --> 00:05:54,534
No Yeong Ju is so frustrating.

93
00:05:57,172 --> 00:05:58,625
There's no going back now.

94
00:06:09,731 --> 00:06:11,391
(Family Register)

95
00:06:29,149 --> 00:06:31,149
(Family Register)

96
00:06:31,150 --> 00:06:33,303
(Name, Na Ji Ni, Mother, Na Se Ri,
Spouse, Lim Ji Hu)

97
00:06:35,711 --> 00:06:38,572
Don't make a big deal out of it.
It's just a piece of paper.

98
00:06:39,412 --> 00:06:40,576
Got anything to eat?

99
00:06:42,535 --> 00:06:43,699
She just says that.

100
00:06:43,701 --> 00:06:45,211
She was thrilled earlier, Mother.

101
00:06:47,119 --> 00:06:49,349
Ji Hu, I can't thank you enough.

102
00:06:49,351 --> 00:06:50,593
I owe it all to you.

103
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:53,894
Not at all.
You've been through so much, Mother.

104
00:06:58,518 --> 00:06:59,518
Mother.

105
00:07:00,754 --> 00:07:03,107
What's this?

106
00:07:06,062 --> 00:07:09,472
Is this mine? Really?

107
00:07:10,919 --> 00:07:14,665
Ji Hu! My goodness!

108
00:07:17,932 --> 00:07:18,932
What's that?

109
00:07:19,985 --> 00:07:21,684
I got one too!

110
00:07:23,872 --> 00:07:27,170
Ji Ni, my mom, and Aunt all have rings,

111
00:07:27,372 --> 00:07:28,848
but you were the only one without one.

112
00:07:28,850 --> 00:07:33,594
You're such a sweetheart!
How did I get so lucky to have you?

113
00:07:33,788 --> 00:07:35,663
Mom, you'll make a habit of that.

114
00:07:35,665 --> 00:07:37,310
You'll make a big mistake later.
Just hold back.

115
00:07:37,864 --> 00:07:38,864
You little brat.

116
00:07:40,692 --> 00:07:43,091
When did you manage to get this?

117
00:07:44,272 --> 00:07:45,403
You must have a lot of money.

118
00:07:45,955 --> 00:07:47,216
I've been saving up.

119
00:07:47,438 --> 00:07:49,524
I also did some stock trading
while I was in England.

120
00:07:49,658 --> 00:07:51,902
By the way,

121
00:07:52,132 --> 00:07:55,066
it seems your family
has always been wealthy.

122
00:07:55,068 --> 00:07:56,449
Just how wealthy are they?

123
00:07:56,769 --> 00:07:58,591
I'm not really sure.

124
00:07:58,922 --> 00:08:01,636
I heard they've owned a lot of ships
since my grandpa's time.

125
00:08:01,717 --> 00:08:03,720
Ships? Like, shipping tycoons?

126
00:08:05,031 --> 00:08:09,352
So that's why Do Hee and her mom
were so desperate to get you!

127
00:08:10,246 --> 00:08:11,498
Mom!

128
00:08:12,589 --> 00:08:13,905
Anyway, thanks.

129
00:08:13,907 --> 00:08:18,125
I prepared some amazing wedding food
and already had it delivered.

130
00:08:20,973 --> 00:08:22,697
Even my hands look prettier now.

131
00:08:37,205 --> 00:08:40,011
- You're back.
- Yes, we're home.

132
00:08:40,189 --> 00:08:42,942
You look worn out. Are you tired?

133
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:44,853
Not at all. Where's Dad?

134
00:08:45,791 --> 00:08:49,667
He suddenly went to Jeju
with Assemblyman Kim for an expo.

135
00:08:49,752 --> 00:08:52,498
He knew you were coming
and was disappointed to miss you.

136
00:08:52,939 --> 00:08:54,645
Mother, we'd like to pay our respects.

137
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:57,218
No, let's wait until your dad gets back.

138
00:08:57,351 --> 00:08:59,042
We already received your formal bow.

139
00:08:59,619 --> 00:09:00,730
Go get some rest.

140
00:09:03,738 --> 00:09:06,666
We should've worn our hanboks,
shouldn't we?

141
00:09:06,922 --> 00:09:09,097
It's fine. We'll do it when Dad gets back.

142
00:09:09,795 --> 00:09:11,007
- Okay.
- Let's go to our room.

143
00:09:24,625 --> 00:09:25,682
Come in.

144
00:09:28,205 --> 00:09:29,382
It's a little cramped, right?

145
00:09:29,862 --> 00:09:32,625
No. We have the living room outside.

146
00:09:33,571 --> 00:09:36,128
But you must've felt a little cramped
in here by yourself.

147
00:09:38,025 --> 00:09:39,872
I like that it's small.

148
00:09:40,238 --> 00:09:41,605
Here's your welcome kiss.

149
00:09:43,805 --> 00:09:44,937
What's that noise?

150
00:09:45,535 --> 00:09:46,535
I wonder what it is.

151
00:09:59,411 --> 00:10:00,946
Was this here before?

152
00:10:01,332 --> 00:10:02,332
No.

153
00:10:09,372 --> 00:10:11,020
Mom, I heard a weird noise from my room...

154
00:10:14,545 --> 00:10:16,865
- Did you do this, Mom?
- Yeah, I did.

155
00:10:17,798 --> 00:10:20,889
My wrists have been bothering me lately,

156
00:10:21,804 --> 00:10:23,388
so I can't hold my phone.

157
00:10:23,471 --> 00:10:27,185
It's not like I can keep yelling
up to the second floor.

158
00:10:27,542 --> 00:10:30,810
And I can't keep climbing the stairs
and hurting my feet.

159
00:10:30,929 --> 00:10:32,457
It's a good idea, isn't it?

160
00:10:32,458 --> 00:10:33,956
It's way too loud.

161
00:10:33,958 --> 00:10:35,231
It startled Ji Ni.

162
00:10:35,232 --> 00:10:37,899
She'll get used to it.
It's just because it's new.

163
00:10:38,358 --> 00:10:40,236
She said she wanted us to get along.

164
00:10:40,405 --> 00:10:42,732
We need a way to communicate, don't we?

165
00:10:42,758 --> 00:10:45,164
When I press this, tell Ji Ni to come.

166
00:10:45,166 --> 00:10:46,304
I'm calling Ji Ni, after all.

167
00:10:46,305 --> 00:10:48,225
Mom, still, this is a bit...

168
00:10:48,227 --> 00:10:51,210
Young people these days
don't like phone calls, do they?

169
00:10:51,212 --> 00:10:53,641
Phone phobia? What a strange term.

170
00:10:53,725 --> 00:10:56,260
I looked into it before deciding.

171
00:10:57,158 --> 00:10:59,437
Calling would be inconvenient.

172
00:10:59,558 --> 00:11:02,592
If I text and she doesn't read it,
I'd have to wait and wait.

173
00:11:02,892 --> 00:11:05,271
Then I'd end up shouting.

174
00:11:05,325 --> 00:11:08,181
I'd be going up and down the stairs.
Am I wrong?

175
00:11:17,185 --> 00:11:18,997
Did you call for me, Mother?

176
00:11:19,030 --> 00:11:21,603
See? Isn't this much neater?

177
00:11:21,705 --> 00:11:24,299
Stop frowning and leave. I called Ji Ni.

178
00:11:35,533 --> 00:11:39,707
How can you look so gloomy
even when you smile?

179
00:11:39,758 --> 00:11:41,531
That's quite a talent.

180
00:11:43,576 --> 00:11:46,387
And now you've completely changed
your expression.

181
00:11:46,852 --> 00:11:48,087
Are you upset?

182
00:11:48,089 --> 00:11:50,325
No, I'm fine.

183
00:11:51,658 --> 00:11:53,352
It may be hard at first,

184
00:11:53,626 --> 00:11:55,614
but put up with it until you adjust.

185
00:11:55,952 --> 00:11:58,249
- Okay.
- This is my house.

186
00:11:58,572 --> 00:12:03,611
I'm the owner,
so don't get too comfortable here.

187
00:12:04,692 --> 00:12:07,989
If you two giggle upstairs like newlyweds,
I'll hear everything.

188
00:12:07,991 --> 00:12:10,102
You insisted on moving in,

189
00:12:10,976 --> 00:12:14,892
so be considerate
and watch yourselves. Understand?

190
00:12:15,122 --> 00:12:16,122
Yes.

191
00:12:17,375 --> 00:12:19,492
Okay. You can go.

192
00:12:20,306 --> 00:12:21,306
Yes.

193
00:12:29,932 --> 00:12:31,066
What did Mom say?

194
00:12:32,228 --> 00:12:34,244
Nothing. Just greetings.

195
00:12:34,322 --> 00:12:35,365
Are you sure?

196
00:12:36,185 --> 00:12:37,898
You can be honest with me.

197
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:39,312
That way, I can help.

198
00:12:40,305 --> 00:12:43,358
When Aunt first moved in here,
Mom sent Ms. Su Yeon to Jeju.

199
00:12:43,925 --> 00:12:46,290
Aunt said she had a hard time
as soon as she moved in.

200
00:12:46,492 --> 00:12:47,734
Really?

201
00:12:49,019 --> 00:12:50,019
She did that on purpose?

202
00:12:50,165 --> 00:12:51,288
I think so.

203
00:12:53,435 --> 00:12:54,627
I see.

204
00:12:55,791 --> 00:12:58,182
Don't worry.
I wasn't raised to be sheltered.

205
00:12:58,305 --> 00:12:59,741
My mom always used to say,

206
00:12:59,785 --> 00:13:01,449
even if the attacker is
a third-degree black belt,

207
00:13:01,456 --> 00:13:03,649
a fifth-degree at taking hits can win.

208
00:13:04,227 --> 00:13:05,426
That sounds like your mom.

209
00:13:06,345 --> 00:13:07,778
Don't just put up with it.

210
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:09,911
Whatever happens, tell me first.

211
00:13:13,429 --> 00:13:14,429
Let's go.

212
00:13:17,031 --> 00:13:18,156
Anything else?

213
00:13:18,452 --> 00:13:20,278
That's all I know.

214
00:13:20,401 --> 00:13:22,012
The owner's son at Pumseonggak.

215
00:13:22,258 --> 00:13:24,133
You said he never went to high school.

216
00:13:24,484 --> 00:13:26,789
So he went to middle school
around here, right?

217
00:13:26,790 --> 00:13:28,012
I suppose so.

218
00:13:28,205 --> 00:13:29,838
I heard it from my nephew too.

219
00:13:29,908 --> 00:13:32,182
He was one of the kids
who used to hang out at the arcade.

220
00:13:32,893 --> 00:13:34,855
Why? Want me to ask around?

221
00:13:35,043 --> 00:13:36,746
I don't know if anyone will remember.

222
00:13:36,812 --> 00:13:38,801
- What about his name?
- His name?

223
00:13:39,212 --> 00:13:42,324
I only heard his nickname. "Iron Bag."

224
00:13:42,411 --> 00:13:45,510
His family owned a Chinese restaurant,
and I heard "Cheol" was in his name.

225
00:13:46,402 --> 00:13:47,687
- "Cheol?"
- Yes.

226
00:13:48,648 --> 00:13:50,733
He went to Seo Chon Middle School, right?

227
00:13:51,492 --> 00:13:53,245
Could you find out what years he attended?

228
00:13:53,312 --> 00:13:54,672
I went to that school too.

229
00:13:54,678 --> 00:13:58,033
Then I'll ask if I can get a copy
of the yearbook.

230
00:13:58,463 --> 00:14:00,690
Really? Thank you.

231
00:14:01,118 --> 00:14:02,946
I really hope they have the yearbook.

232
00:14:09,351 --> 00:14:11,705
You already paid me last time.

233
00:14:12,313 --> 00:14:14,185
This is a different favor.

234
00:14:14,505 --> 00:14:16,375
I was actually planning
to come see you anyway.

235
00:14:17,232 --> 00:14:19,969
Please, just find out his full name.

236
00:14:20,104 --> 00:14:22,555
Okay. I'll call when I find out.

237
00:14:25,078 --> 00:14:27,280
I was just delivering rice cakes
next door.

238
00:14:28,727 --> 00:14:29,727
Take care.

239
00:14:30,932 --> 00:14:31,932
Goodbye.

240
00:14:42,659 --> 00:14:43,725
What took you so long?

241
00:14:43,942 --> 00:14:45,418
You're 30 minutes late.

242
00:14:45,791 --> 00:14:47,118
I'll pay you by the hour.

243
00:14:47,143 --> 00:14:48,227
I'm expensive.

244
00:14:48,252 --> 00:14:50,829
I'm not some worker you can hire
for 10.32 dollars an hour.

245
00:14:51,225 --> 00:14:52,443
I'll buy you beef.

246
00:14:52,587 --> 00:14:53,660
Beef...

247
00:14:54,327 --> 00:14:55,844
I was going to stay up all night anyway.

248
00:15:10,387 --> 00:15:11,960
(Director, it's Do Hee!)

249
00:15:15,637 --> 00:15:16,768
Hi, Director!

250
00:15:17,154 --> 00:15:18,271
How have you been?

251
00:15:18,472 --> 00:15:20,445
You're not still mad at me, are you?

252
00:15:21,125 --> 00:15:23,535
Just wanted to say
I hope you're doing well.

253
00:15:24,579 --> 00:15:26,315
I haven't been beaten to death,

254
00:15:26,612 --> 00:15:29,322
and these days, I'm going with Dad
to meet important people,

255
00:15:29,346 --> 00:15:30,884
learning how high society works.

256
00:15:32,012 --> 00:15:33,370
I'm curious. Keep reading.

257
00:15:33,964 --> 00:15:36,124
Hey! Why are you sneaking
a look over my shoulder?

258
00:15:37,484 --> 00:15:38,766
Well done, little brother.

259
00:15:39,018 --> 00:15:40,819
With that hand that just touched
a dirty rag...

260
00:15:41,124 --> 00:15:42,692
I'm not eating meat. I'm leaving.

261
00:15:42,717 --> 00:15:44,270
Seriously.

262
00:15:45,551 --> 00:15:47,242
Look at my boys, hanging out together.

263
00:15:49,049 --> 00:15:50,283
You two seem to be getting along.

264
00:15:50,308 --> 00:15:53,104
Getting along?
He's just picking on me again.

265
00:15:53,232 --> 00:15:55,028
Don't worry about your younger son.

266
00:15:55,232 --> 00:15:57,272
I think he'll stop dating
and focus on work now.

267
00:15:57,296 --> 00:15:58,312
Really?

268
00:15:58,337 --> 00:15:59,878
- Three coffees, please.
- Sure.

269
00:15:59,903 --> 00:16:02,141
There's no privacy
in this ridiculous family.

270
00:16:03,571 --> 00:16:05,333
I told you not to call it that.

271
00:16:05,445 --> 00:16:07,626
I gave up my youth
to keep this family together.

272
00:16:11,532 --> 00:16:12,532
I'm heading out.

273
00:16:12,556 --> 00:16:14,003
Okay. Take care.

274
00:16:20,939 --> 00:16:21,939
Enjoy your drink.

275
00:16:22,396 --> 00:16:24,631
- Good work, my son.
- Thanks.

276
00:16:37,052 --> 00:16:39,246
It's me. It's been a while.

277
00:16:40,692 --> 00:16:42,490
Sorry I haven't been in touch.

278
00:16:42,759 --> 00:16:43,972
Do you happen to...

279
00:16:44,689 --> 00:16:47,118
keep in touch with anyone
from middle school?

280
00:16:49,757 --> 00:16:51,515
I'm looking for someone.

281
00:16:52,206 --> 00:16:54,549
He's five or six years older than us.

282
00:17:00,391 --> 00:17:01,537
I'll give it to you tomorrow.

283
00:17:01,694 --> 00:17:03,694
I'll make sure you get it. I promise.

284
00:17:04,059 --> 00:17:06,510
The money's coming in tomorrow. I swear.

285
00:17:06,852 --> 00:17:08,130
By the end of this week.

286
00:17:08,957 --> 00:17:10,873
I'll get in touch.

287
00:17:16,297 --> 00:17:18,025
That gaming-obsessed bastard.

288
00:17:24,545 --> 00:17:26,172
Clean this place up.

289
00:17:45,912 --> 00:17:46,912
Hey!

290
00:17:47,192 --> 00:17:48,338
I got beaten up because of you!

291
00:17:48,363 --> 00:17:50,052
Hurry up and bring me the money.

292
00:17:50,652 --> 00:17:52,860
I know exactly
where your daughter got married.

293
00:17:52,958 --> 00:17:54,878
I know her studio
and the publishing house too!

294
00:17:54,903 --> 00:17:56,218
Just try going after my daughter.

295
00:17:56,312 --> 00:17:59,295
If you do, it'll be the end of both of us.

296
00:17:59,532 --> 00:18:01,699
I'm not afraid of you either.

297
00:18:02,365 --> 00:18:03,842
You rotten bastard!

298
00:18:07,151 --> 00:18:08,151
Fine.

299
00:18:08,327 --> 00:18:10,537
It's all or nothing now.

300
00:18:29,254 --> 00:18:31,345
I'm sorry. I should've come earlier.

301
00:18:31,491 --> 00:18:32,624
Did you do all this?

302
00:18:32,648 --> 00:18:33,648
We did it together.

303
00:18:34,824 --> 00:18:36,824
That looks delicious.

304
00:18:41,783 --> 00:18:42,783
It's delicious.

305
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:46,862
Smells wonderful.

306
00:18:48,311 --> 00:18:50,131
It's even nicer seeing you here.

307
00:18:50,874 --> 00:18:51,985
I feel the same.

308
00:18:53,857 --> 00:18:56,255
Why didn't you ask me to join you?

309
00:18:56,280 --> 00:18:58,428
I was just about to come ask you.

310
00:18:58,452 --> 00:18:59,562
When?

311
00:18:59,885 --> 00:19:02,449
- After you've eaten and are having tea?
- Mom, why...

312
00:19:03,652 --> 00:19:04,764
We just got here too.

313
00:19:04,788 --> 00:19:05,944
Sun Kyung.

314
00:19:06,552 --> 00:19:09,594
With a new family member here,
the table looks so much brighter.

315
00:19:10,992 --> 00:19:12,685
Our dear Ji Ni is lovely, isn't she?

316
00:19:15,697 --> 00:19:17,231
Why is it so salty?

317
00:19:17,772 --> 00:19:18,888
It tasted fine to me.

318
00:19:18,918 --> 00:19:20,518
Maybe my mouth just tastes bitter.

319
00:19:21,858 --> 00:19:22,858
Won't you eat some?

320
00:19:22,978 --> 00:19:24,694
I'd eat it if it tasted any good.

321
00:19:24,938 --> 00:19:26,824
Get me a glass of water.

322
00:19:27,253 --> 00:19:28,253
Okay.

323
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:30,553
- I'll get it.
- No.

324
00:19:30,578 --> 00:19:32,018
Give me a chance to impress her.

325
00:19:42,058 --> 00:19:43,356
Here she goes again.

326
00:19:45,044 --> 00:19:46,967
Can't you speak up when she does that?

327
00:19:46,992 --> 00:19:48,227
Why do you keep quiet?

328
00:19:48,252 --> 00:19:50,196
Can't you bring yourself to confront her?

329
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:52,858
She said her mouth tastes bitter.

330
00:19:53,698 --> 00:19:55,689
That could be why the food tastes off.

331
00:20:06,571 --> 00:20:08,417
Wait. Be patient.

332
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:10,463
It took me a long time too.

333
00:20:10,488 --> 00:20:11,985
Isn't she going too far?

334
00:20:12,284 --> 00:20:14,511
She hasn't smiled at Ji Ni even once.

335
00:20:15,772 --> 00:20:17,150
We never should've lived here.

336
00:20:17,592 --> 00:20:19,341
We should've had our own place
with her mom.

337
00:20:19,366 --> 00:20:21,029
I understand how you feel,

338
00:20:21,333 --> 00:20:23,262
but you need to handle this
more carefully.

339
00:20:23,892 --> 00:20:25,500
If you take sides,

340
00:20:25,743 --> 00:20:28,348
both sides will get mad at you.

341
00:20:28,361 --> 00:20:29,874
Then what am I supposed to do?

342
00:20:29,959 --> 00:20:31,268
Swing back and forth.

343
00:20:31,272 --> 00:20:33,741
Side with Mom in the living room
and your wife in the bedroom.

344
00:20:33,778 --> 00:20:35,198
And if you get that backward?

345
00:20:35,288 --> 00:20:36,458
It's a nightmare.

346
00:20:36,639 --> 00:20:40,305
This is a trade secret.
I shouldn't be sharing it for free.

347
00:20:42,139 --> 00:20:43,558
Swing back and forth.

348
00:20:44,057 --> 00:20:46,713
Mom in the living room,
Ji Ni in the bedroom.

349
00:20:46,714 --> 00:20:47,835
That's right.

350
00:20:57,800 --> 00:20:59,417
- I'll go.
- Okay.

351
00:20:59,947 --> 00:21:02,128
Sleep tight, Ji Ni.

352
00:21:16,624 --> 00:21:19,232
My mom showed up on our honeymoon,

353
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:21,936
and his mom can buzz us in our bedroom.

354
00:21:25,176 --> 00:21:28,096
This is tough.

355
00:21:35,118 --> 00:21:36,621
Mom, did you need me?

356
00:21:37,757 --> 00:21:39,021
Why are you...

357
00:21:40,542 --> 00:21:42,807
Never mind. I pressed it by mistake.

358
00:21:43,024 --> 00:21:44,200
Okay.

359
00:21:46,631 --> 00:21:47,870
Are you cold?

360
00:21:48,487 --> 00:21:50,287
- What?
- Should I check the heating?

361
00:21:50,792 --> 00:21:52,704
No.

362
00:21:54,617 --> 00:21:55,927
I'm fine.

363
00:21:57,045 --> 00:21:59,114
Is something wrong? Are you unwell?

364
00:21:59,115 --> 00:22:01,499
What? No.

365
00:22:01,584 --> 00:22:03,114
I'm okay. Never mind.

366
00:22:04,701 --> 00:22:05,701
Good night.

367
00:22:24,731 --> 00:22:25,994
Wait.

368
00:22:26,497 --> 00:22:27,605
Stay still.

369
00:22:40,871 --> 00:22:43,137
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

370
00:22:43,220 --> 00:22:44,517
I can rest tomorrow.

371
00:22:47,550 --> 00:22:48,997
Go back to sleep.

372
00:22:54,718 --> 00:22:56,356
Seriously...

373
00:23:09,758 --> 00:23:11,031
Did you need me?

374
00:23:11,655 --> 00:23:13,338
About this buzzer...

375
00:23:13,821 --> 00:23:16,671
Didn't I tell you it was meant for you?

376
00:23:16,932 --> 00:23:19,022
Then why do you keep sending Ji Hu?

377
00:23:20,052 --> 00:23:21,179
Are you trying to pick a fight with me?

378
00:23:21,203 --> 00:23:23,232
No. Ji Hu...

379
00:23:25,151 --> 00:23:26,267
I'm sorry.

380
00:23:26,365 --> 00:23:28,122
I'll come right away from now on.

381
00:23:29,592 --> 00:23:32,232
I'm so hungry. I didn't have dinner.

382
00:23:32,352 --> 00:23:33,570
Go make me something to eat.

383
00:23:34,667 --> 00:23:35,874
Now?

384
00:23:37,150 --> 00:23:40,228
Okay. Give me a moment.

385
00:23:52,425 --> 00:23:54,258
I wasn't sure what you'd like.

386
00:23:55,790 --> 00:23:58,249
- Don't we have any blood sausage?
- Blood sausage?

387
00:24:00,457 --> 00:24:01,674
Never mind. You can go.

388
00:24:02,124 --> 00:24:03,666
I'll decide what I want to eat.

389
00:24:04,755 --> 00:24:05,755
Okay.

390
00:24:28,072 --> 00:24:29,072
Ji Ni.

391
00:24:29,481 --> 00:24:31,091
Why aren't you sleeping in your room?

392
00:24:33,155 --> 00:24:35,587
- Is it morning already?
- Were you up all night?

393
00:24:36,151 --> 00:24:38,159
I could hear the buzzer from my room.

394
00:24:38,592 --> 00:24:40,525
What on earth is that thing?

395
00:24:42,118 --> 00:24:44,155
Let me help with breakfast.

396
00:24:44,179 --> 00:24:45,179
Give me a moment.

397
00:25:05,005 --> 00:25:06,837
Why are you being so childish?

398
00:25:08,226 --> 00:25:09,344
What? Watch your tone.

399
00:25:09,412 --> 00:25:10,670
You heard me.

400
00:25:11,204 --> 00:25:13,421
I'm saying this as someone who went
to school with you.

401
00:25:13,474 --> 00:25:16,471
If you want respect, act your age.

402
00:25:16,692 --> 00:25:19,040
You're a mother-in-law. Act like one.

403
00:25:19,262 --> 00:25:21,475
You're behaving like a little kid.

404
00:25:21,522 --> 00:25:22,522
You...

405
00:25:22,887 --> 00:25:25,167
Are you out of your mind?
I'm your senior in-law.

406
00:25:25,211 --> 00:25:28,091
Who puts a buzzer
in the newlyweds' bedroom?

407
00:25:28,572 --> 00:25:30,444
Even I can hear it from my room.

408
00:25:30,845 --> 00:25:32,851
They were up and down all night.

409
00:25:33,838 --> 00:25:37,720
I'll tell everyone at our next reunion
how childish and vulgar you're being.

410
00:25:37,744 --> 00:25:39,472
What? Vulgar?

411
00:25:39,473 --> 00:25:42,175
Yes. Vulgar and pathetic.

412
00:25:42,745 --> 00:25:44,555
Please, just act your age.

413
00:25:44,579 --> 00:25:45,758
I'm embarrassed for you.

414
00:25:48,938 --> 00:25:49,938
That woman...

415
00:26:02,825 --> 00:26:05,621
How could you be so harsh with her?

416
00:26:06,558 --> 00:26:07,901
How was I being harsh?

417
00:26:08,118 --> 00:26:10,907
You heard that buzzer too, Sa Bin.
It rang all night.

418
00:26:10,932 --> 00:26:12,668
Sun Kyung's being childish.

419
00:26:12,779 --> 00:26:14,698
I know she is.

420
00:26:15,132 --> 00:26:17,021
But you could've said it more nicely.

421
00:26:18,161 --> 00:26:19,180
Sa Bin.

422
00:26:19,205 --> 00:26:21,678
I was harsh with Sun Kyung
when we got married,

423
00:26:21,703 --> 00:26:23,044
and I still regret it.

424
00:26:23,147 --> 00:26:25,211
I love and respect you so much,

425
00:26:25,235 --> 00:26:26,636
so I can't believe...

426
00:26:27,945 --> 00:26:30,609
you'd say such cruel things
and hurt my family.

427
00:26:30,634 --> 00:26:34,220
What did I do that was so wrong?

428
00:26:34,531 --> 00:26:38,110
I was trying to keep Ji Ni
from suffering the way I did.

429
00:26:47,959 --> 00:26:50,319
She's not the Yeong Ju I knew.

430
00:26:51,596 --> 00:26:52,652
She's changed.

431
00:26:56,252 --> 00:26:57,410
I don't have money.

432
00:26:57,750 --> 00:26:59,050
I don't have any!

433
00:26:59,225 --> 00:27:01,277
I said I'd come.
Did I say I'd bring money?

434
00:27:01,302 --> 00:27:02,964
Seriously!

435
00:27:04,698 --> 00:27:06,461
I told you I needed money, didn't I?

436
00:27:06,745 --> 00:27:08,825
I told you my family was ruined
because of you!

437
00:27:13,705 --> 00:27:14,971
Prove it.

438
00:27:14,995 --> 00:27:16,816
Prove that I'm the reason!

439
00:27:16,841 --> 00:27:18,391
You, seriously...

440
00:27:18,972 --> 00:27:21,847
Should I tell that family everything
and go down with you?

441
00:27:21,871 --> 00:27:22,871
Do it.

442
00:27:22,896 --> 00:27:24,032
Yes, do it.

443
00:27:24,122 --> 00:27:26,620
Who would believe you?
You're the one who hit him.

444
00:27:26,684 --> 00:27:29,614
You ruined his leg and ran away.

445
00:27:29,639 --> 00:27:33,034
You even told the police
no one had taken the motorcycle out.

446
00:27:33,059 --> 00:27:35,730
You'd already committed a hit-and-run,
hadn't you?

447
00:27:35,892 --> 00:27:38,306
So why are you trying to involve me?

448
00:27:38,725 --> 00:27:40,137
I admit I hit him.

449
00:27:40,605 --> 00:27:44,246
But you saw me hit him
and just drove away.

450
00:27:44,491 --> 00:27:46,419
Then you told us to run away.

451
00:27:46,444 --> 00:27:48,326
That accident happened because of you!

452
00:27:48,959 --> 00:27:50,690
Yet you claim you're not involved?

453
00:27:51,814 --> 00:27:52,814
Fine.

454
00:27:53,398 --> 00:27:54,605
Let's go see that family.

455
00:27:55,309 --> 00:27:56,499
Let me go!

456
00:27:57,344 --> 00:27:58,711
I'll apologize to them...

457
00:27:59,314 --> 00:28:01,457
and accept punishment,
even if it's too late to prosecute.

458
00:28:02,945 --> 00:28:04,550
Will you still be able to rest easy?

459
00:28:05,592 --> 00:28:07,845
Will things still be okay
between you and that family?

460
00:28:51,098 --> 00:28:54,556
(Family Register)

461
00:28:54,580 --> 00:28:56,261
It's been a while.
I heard you needed a writer.

462
00:28:56,285 --> 00:28:57,901
- I'm not accepting your application.
- I got divorced.

463
00:28:57,926 --> 00:29:00,146
- I wanted to date you properly.
- But you're a mom.

464
00:29:00,171 --> 00:29:01,685
I guess I have no luck with mothers.

465
00:29:01,710 --> 00:29:03,592
How are you always so witty?

466
00:29:03,617 --> 00:29:06,132
How can I smile when she says
even my smile looks sad?

467
00:29:06,157 --> 00:29:07,837
I can only leave after paying off
the 200,000 dollars I owe.

468
00:29:07,862 --> 00:29:09,182
Do you think you were scammed?

469
00:29:09,207 --> 00:29:10,508
I'll do what I can to help.

470
00:29:10,532 --> 00:29:12,408
- They say it's him.
- The motorcycle rider?

471
00:29:12,433 --> 00:29:13,988
Should I just kill him?

472
00:29:15,600 --> 00:29:17,600
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
